#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:2
msgid "Triaging an issue — how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:4
msgid ""
"Issue triage helps ROS contributors turn incoming bug reports and "
"enhancement requests into clear, actionable work. This article explains how "
"to find, check, reproduce, assign, and label issues in ROS repositories. "
"With this information, you'll be able to route issues to the right place, "
"with correct information, and prepare them for work by developers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Area: community | Content-type: how-to | Experience: beginner, "
"intermediate, expert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:12
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:15
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:17
msgid "We welcome anyone to triage issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:19
msgid ""
"**Code issue trackers**: in a repository under the `ROS organisation "
"<https://github.com/orgs/ros2/repositories>`__ or elsewhere on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Documentation issue tracker**: `ROS documentation repository <https://"
"github.com/ros2/ros2_documentation/issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Catch-all issue tracker**: `top level ROS repository <https://github.com/"
"ros2/ros2>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:24
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:26
msgid "There are no prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:29
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:32
msgid "1 Finding an issue to triage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:34
msgid ""
"We encourage contributors to look at incoming issues on ROS repositories and "
"triage the problems that users are having:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:36
msgid ""
"To find code issues for triage, review the issues list of a repository under "
"the `ROS organization <https://github.com/orgs/ros2/repositories>`__, for "
"example the issues list in the `ROS CLI repository <https://github.com/ros2/"
"ros2cli/issues/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:37
msgid ""
"To find documentation issues for triage, review the issues list in the `ROS "
"documentation repository <https://github.com/ros2/ros2_documentation>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:38
msgid ""
"If you're not sure where to start, review the issues list in the `top level "
"ROS repository <https://github.com/ros2/ros2>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:40
msgid ""
"When you have identified an issue for triage, add a comment to the issue to "
"say that you are looking into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:43
msgid "2 Confirming and reproducing the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:45
msgid ""
"When you have found an issue to triage, confirm that the issue is genuinely "
"an issue (a bug or a request for enhancement) and has been created with the "
"expected information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:47
msgid ""
"For more information about the information the reporter of the issue is "
"expected to provide, see :doc:`./Reporting-an-issue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:49
msgid ""
"If the issue ``Description`` is actually posing a question, close the issue "
"and add a comment directing the user to the `Robotics Stack Exchange "
"<https://robotics.stackexchange.com/>`__ to get help with their question."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:50
msgid ""
"If the issue looks like a genuine issue (bug or enhancement), but is not "
"relevant to the repository it has been raised in, transfer the issue to the "
"appropriate ROS repository (`see the GitHub documentation for guidance about "
"how to transfer between repositories <https://docs.github.com/en/issues/"
"tracking-your-work-with-issues/administering-issues/transferring-an-issue-to-"
"another-repository>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:51
msgid ""
"If the issue appears to be a valid but lacks sufficient details to replicate "
"the environment (for example, the host operating system, platform, RMW "
"implementation, ROS distro, and offending code) please request that author "
"provide additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:52
msgid ""
"If the issue is a bug, try to reproduce the bug using the provided steps — "
"if you cannot reproduce the bug, add a comment to the reporter asking for "
"clarification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:55
msgid "3 Assigning and labelling the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:57
msgid ""
"After you've confirmed the issue is a genuine issue, and reproduced it, "
"assign and label the issue appropriately to allow work on the issue to begin "
"by a developer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:59
msgid "Assign the issue to the maintainer for the ROS repository in question."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:60
msgid "Label the issue as a ``bug`` or ``enhancement``, as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:61
msgid ""
"If this issue is a request for a new feature, label the issue with ``help-"
"wanted``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:62
msgid ""
"If the reporter has not provided enough information to determine the cause "
"of the problem, label the issue as ``more-information-needed`` and leave a "
"comment for the reporter, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:64
msgid "What you have tried while investigating the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:65
msgid "In what way the information supplied was insufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Triaging-an-issue.rst:66
msgid ""
"Any suggestions you may have about what additional information is needed."
msgstr ""

